    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nThe surface tilts at $\\tan\\theta = a/g$. The height difference across length $L$ is $\\Delta h = L \\tan\\theta = \\frac{L a}{g}$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nLength $L = 1.10\\text{ m}$, acceleration $a = 2.40\\text{ m/s}^2$, $g = 9.8\\text{ m/s}^2$.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\n\\Delta h = \\frac{L a}{g}\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Tilt angle: $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{2.40}{9.8}$.\n2. Height difference: $\\Delta h = L \\tan\\theta = \\frac{1.10 \\times 2.40}{9.8} = 0.2694\\text{ m} = 26.94\\text{ cm}$.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 26.94 cm\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nWater level rises by $\\Delta h / 2$ at the back and drops by $\\Delta h / 2$ at the front.",
